d $(4,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506539 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506539 #edb/ref 1069 "q-8002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506539 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506539 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $5{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=16$ intersects the line $y=x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506539 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48e55e9e-f8d4-5cc0-b60c-cb504ca3f4b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506539 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278361" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1071 "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8c404e97-7fab-5c9d-b54c-fbf58817ca24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506566 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ y & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,4)$ and $(0,-4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-8010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506585 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-{y}^{2}=1$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c693f3f3-9251-58ce-8006-d594413ed6b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506585 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x,$ we first replace $y$ with $\\frac{1}{3}x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 0 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the last equation is a false statement, we conclude that the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
